ALGORITHM: Generate Parentheses

1. Start.

2. Create an empty list called ans.

3. Define a recursive DFS function with:
       left
       right
       current string

4. If:
       left == n AND right == n

   Then:
       Add the current string to ans.
       Return.

5. If:
       left < n

   Then:
       Add "(" to the current string.
       Increment left.
       Recursively call DFS.

6. If:
       right < left

   Then:
       Add ")" to the current string.
       Increment right.
       Recursively call DFS.

7. Backtrack after each recursive call.

8. Continue until all valid combinations
   have been generated.

9. Return ans.

TIME COMPLEXITY:
O(4^n / √n)

SPACE COMPLEXITY:
O(n) excluding the output.
